 "text": "Figure D. The shipped operating point, on the detector's own two knobs. Each marker is the full v1.49.1 chain re-run at one setting over the same 26 hand-labelled tiles from 13 specimens, scored at 0 px tolerance and pooled over pixels. The dotted line is the no-information floor: the precision a mask of the same per-tile area would score with its pixels scattered at random, which is 0.0242 at the shipped area and 0.0297 for a mask that covers everything. The grey curve drops one tile, an off-specimen void that owns most of the corpus's false positives, and it moves precision by about 0.37 \u2014 further than either knob does. That single tile is also why absolute_dark_thresh=0 appears to win on the pooled curve (IoU 0.4522 against 0.3344 at the shipped 10) and loses on the other 25 (0.5056 against 0.5329); the shipped setting of 10 is unchanged.",
 "tolerance_px": 0
